# CIRO Backend — Production Upgrade Implementation Plan

## Summary

The CIRO Firebase backend has 9 identified gaps that prevent it from being production-ready. These issues fall into three natural dependency tiers: **data quality** (what we feed the system), **operational logic** (how the system acts on data), and **resilience** (what happens when things go wrong). The plan below executes these tiers in order so each phase's output is valid input for the next.

All changes are confined to `d:\CIRO\backend\index.js` unless a new helper file is explicitly noted.

---

## Phase 1 — Intelligence & Schema
*Issues addressed: #1 (Location Extraction), #8 (Restrictive Enums), #6 (logSwarmActivity metadata)*

**Goal:** Improve the quality of data entering the pipeline. No data is useful if we can't locate it, classify it correctly, or trace which agent produced it.

### Changes

#### [MODIFY] [index.js](file:///d:/CIRO/backend/index.js) — `logSwarmActivity`
- Add a `log_level` parameter (`"info"` | `"warning"` | `"critical"`) with a default of `"info"`.
- Write `log_level` as a field to the `SwarmActivity` Firestore doc so the mobile frontend can color-code cards.
- The existing `try/catch` already exists — no structural change needed here, just the new field.

#### [MODIFY] [index.js](file:///d:/CIRO/backend/index.js) — `ingestionAgent` prompt & schema
- Expand the `event_type` enum from 4 values to 9:
  `flood`, `heatwave`, `accident`, `fire`, `earthquake`, `stampede`, `structural_collapse`, `riot`, `unknown`
- Add a new `inferred_location` object to the response schema:
  ```
  {
    lat: FLOAT,   // derived from text hints (e.g. "G-10 Markaz")
    lng: FLOAT,
    confidence: INTEGER  // 0–100, how certain the model is
    locality_name: STRING  // human-readable place name extracted
  }
  ```
- Update the system instruction to instruct the model to use Pakistani city geography (Islamabad sectors, Karachi zones, Lahore areas) as a reference when inferring coordinates from text.
- Pass `inferred_location` forward into the `StagedSignals` document.

**Dependencies for Phase 2:** `StagedSignals` docs will now carry `normalized_data.inferred_location`, which the Analysis Agent needs for deduplication.

