## Phase 3 — Reliability & Notifications
*Issues addressed: #7 (Dead-Letter Handling), #9 (Webhook/Notification Fan-out)*

**Goal:** Ensure no signal is silently dropped, and that a pluggable notification scaffold is in place for Expo Push.

### Changes

#### [MODIFY] [index.js](file:///d:/CIRO/backend/index.js) — All four agents (Gemini call sites)
**Dead-letter queue (Issue #7):**
- Wrap every `ai.models.generateContent(...)` call in a dedicated helper `callGeminiWithRetry(model, prompt, config)`:
  - Attempts the call up to **2 times** with a 3-second backoff.
  - On final failure, writes a document to a `FailedSignals` collection:
    ```
    {
      original_collection: "IncomingSignals" | "StagedSignals" | ...,
      original_id: <doc id>,
      error_message: <string>,
      failed_at: <timestamp>,
      status: "failed",
      retry_count: 2
    }
    ```
  - Logs a `log_level: "critical"` swarm activity.
  - Returns `null` so each agent can short-circuit gracefully instead of throwing.

#### [NEW] `notificationAgent` — Firestore-triggered function
**Notification fan-out scaffold (Issue #9):**
- Triggered on `onDocumentCreated("ActiveCrises/{crisisId}")`.
- Reads the new crisis doc to extract `type`, `severity`, `location.locality_name`.
- Constructs a push notification payload:
  ```json
  {
    "title": "⚠️ Crisis Declared: <type>",
    "body": "<locality_name> — Severity <severity>/10",
    "data": { "crisisId": "<id>", "screen": "CrisisDetail" }
  }
  ```
- Fetches all tokens from a `PushTokens` Firestore collection (field: `expoPushToken`).
- **Scaffold only:** The actual HTTP call to `https://exp.host/--/api/v2/push/send` is wrapped in a clearly marked `// TODO: PLUG IN EXPO PUSH HERE` comment block, matching the architecture pattern from the AI Lawyers Diary project.
- Includes commented-out batch chunking logic (Expo requires ≤100 tokens per call).

